er model is given (the `otherProvider` logic). This preserves the existing behavior where a missing finder model picks the other provider relative to the verifier."]}],"originalFile":"# Ticket 01: Starter role choice prefactor\n\n## Plan\n\nThe ticket is a refactor with no user-visible change. Key changes:\n\n1. Add suggested model ID constants to `src/config/defaults.ts`\n2. Introduce a `RoleChoice` type (built-in provider + model) as input to `starter()`\n3. Refactor `starter()` to accept `RoleChoice` per role instead of two model strings\n4. Update `UnplaceableModelError` example text to use the new constants\n5. Map flags in `init.ts` onto the new `RoleChoice` input\n6. `init` checks config existence right after resolving git toplevel (early check)\n\n## Checklist items\n\n- [ ] init with both model flags writes same config as before\n- [ ] init with one flag / none writes same placement as before\n- [ ] Unplaceable model flag is still a usage error, writes nothing\n- [ ] init in dir with existing .roast.json fails, leaves file unchanged\n- [ ] Starter output for flag-only input loads through config loader same as before\n\n## Notes\n\n- The existing tests already cover most of these behaviors\n- The refactor must keep all existing tests passing\n- New type: `RoleChoice = { provider:string; model:string }`\n- `starter()` signature changes from `(finderModel, verifierModel)` to `(finder:RoleChoice, verifier:RoleChoice)`\n- Need a `choiceFromFlag()` helper that uses `placeModel` / `otherProvider`\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01J3gD3XEhXLpNW93d951LQU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
